Journal, Phase 4

The Singleton made it convenient for multiple subsystems to access the same configuration without having to pass the configuration object into every class. 
However, Singleton can create problems because it uses global state and can create hidden dependencies that make testing harder. 
A Singleton is appropriate when there should truly only be one shared instance, such as a game configuration manager.
Dependency Injection is better when classes need to be easier to test, more flexible, or use different configurations.



